    "title": "Extravagant Contemporary on 120 Acres Along the Williams River, in Great Barrington - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Jamie Larson ,\n13 hours ago Built in 2010 on nearly 120 acres of protected land off a private road in Great Barrington, 250 Long Pond Road is an architecturally significant contemporary designed by Steven Haas, constructed of steel, glass, concrete, and wood, with German Sorpetaler sliding glass walls and expansive IPE hardwood decks that run the length of the building. The design intent, developed by the owner and Haas together, was to bring the outdoor magic indoors and create a feeling of immersion in nature. Read full article",
